.TH XUR.STD.JSON 7 "2026-10-29" "xur 0.1.2" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.json \- JSON serialisation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::json;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::json
parses JSON text into Xur values and serialises Xur values back to
JSON. Objects become records, arrays become lists, numbers become
integers or floats, strings remain strings, booleans remain booleans,
and
.B null
becomes
.BR None .
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B parse(text) -> Result<value, str>
Parse a JSON string. Returns the parsed value or an error.
.TP
.B stringify(value) -> str
Serialise a value to a JSON string.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::json;
use std::io;

fn main() -> Result<()> {
    let data = json::parse("{\\"name\\": \\"xur\\", \\"version\\": 1}")?;
    io::println("name: {}", data.name);
    io::println("{}", json::stringify(data));
    Ok(())
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.fs (7)
